# Two tool calls in a single conversational turn.
#
# What this DOES verify: both bash tool calls complete and their stdout
# tokens land on the grid. Tests tool_use id correlation and
# tool_result wiring across two distinct calls.
#
# What this does NOT verify: that the model actually issued them in
# parallel (a single tool_use block per assistant message). The grid
# text dump can't distinguish a parallel block of two tool_use entries
# from two serial assistant turns. To audit parallelism, inspect the
# session JSONL the simulator copies to the run's artifact dir as
# session.jsonl: parallel runs show two `tool_use` events with the
# same parent assistant turn between two `assistant` markers.

spawn ./zig-out/bin/zag
wait_text /Welcome to zag/
wait_idle 500ms
send "In one turn, run two bash calls: 'echo 8K-A-rap-gaz | rev' and 'echo 5Y-B-rap-gaz | rev'. Both verbatim, each its own tool call." <Enter>
wait_text /zag-par-A-K8/ 60s
wait_text /zag-par-B-Y5/ 60s
snapshot final
send "/quit" <Enter>
wait_exit
